    "findings": [],
    "reason": "The four-line check in projectPeopleProduct is the shared website/ebook scoped projection, so both products fail before family-graph, schema, and site-index emission when any scoped cluster\u2019s canonicalReferences([]) is empty. references are mention-derived unit rows, not claims or derived inverse family, which matches the live father (named/office/family claims, mentions=[], son compound span). Reconstruction, mapping, overrides, and existing throws are unchanged. The new test is a true prior-behavior regression: same fixture would have published a zero-excerpt father; restore path still requires every scoped person to have references. Merged scoped members still pass if any in-scope member has mentions; outside-only mentions correctly fail. Global compile remaining silent is in-scope for this gate."
